# CHANGELOG.md merge=union
#
# A safety net, not the fix. The fix is changelog.d/ — one file per
# change, so two pull requests cannot touch the same lines at all. See
# changelog.d/README.md.
#
# This line still earns its place for the merges that do touch this file
# directly: a release assembly, a correction, a branch cut before the
# fragments landed. `union` is a built-in git driver that keeps the lines
# from both sides instead of stopping at a conflict.
#
# Two limits, both measured rather than assumed:
#
#   - GitHub's server-side merge does NOT honour it. The same merge that
#     git resolves cleanly from the command line was still handed to a
#     human in the web conflict editor. That is precisely why the real
#     fix had to be changelog.d/ rather than this line.
#
#   - union never honours a deletion. When one side removes a line and
#     the other keeps it, the line survives. Removing something from this
#     file therefore belongs in its own commit on main, not in a branch
#     racing another one.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
